          { label: 'Europe', href: '/europe/' },
          { label: 'Shipping from China to Denmark' },
        ]}
      />
      <span class="badge badge--amber">September 2026 updated</span>
      <h1>Shipping from China to Denmark: cost, transit &amp; duty</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        A one-page freight brief for importers moving cargo from Shanghai, Ningbo-Zhoushan, Shenzhen
        and the wider China origin set to Aarhus, Copenhagen and the Danish market — with the
        Aarhus-vs-Copenhagen geography, the roughly 32–40-day sea window via the Cape plus an inland
        leg, the 20–24-day rail alternative, EU common duty plus a flat 25% VAT, the DKK peg to the
        euro, the EORI gate, and the hidden destination charges that shape the Danish landed cost.
