      <h2>4. Sea vs rail vs air: Denmark&rsquo;s true door-to-door decision</h2>
      <p>
        Denmark has its own deep-sea port, but the port choice is split by geography: <strong>Aarhus on the
        Kattegat</strong> (reached from the North Sea via the Skagerrak) serves Jutland, while
        <strong>Copenhagen on the Øresund</strong> serves Zealand. The honest comparison is therefore
        <strong>door-to-door, not port-to-port</strong>: roughly <strong>32–40 days</strong> by sea to
        Aarhus plus <strong>~1–2 days</strong> inland, against roughly <strong>20–24 days</strong> by rail
        via the Hamburg corridor.
      </p>

      <DataTable
