      and Xiamen provide northern/southeast alternatives. The destination side is Denmark&rsquo;s two-port
      geometry plus one interior hub: <strong>Aarhus (DKAAR)</strong> on the Kattegat is the mainline
      gate for Jutland, <strong>Copenhagen (DKCPH)</strong> is the Øresund/Baltic gate for Zealand, and
      <strong>Fredericia (DKFRH)</strong> is the Little Belt logistics and energy hub between Jutland and
